<title>UK: UK's house prices rise 1.3 pct in Nov - Nationwide.</title>
<headline>UK's house prices rise 1.3 pct in Nov - Nationwide.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Nationwide Building Society</p>
<p>released the following UK house price data -</p>
<p> HOUSE PRICES (index base Q1 1983=100)  Nov	Oct    Nov,95</p>
<p> Monthly index (s/adj)			111.3   109.8  102.6</p>
<p> Monthly change (s/adj, in pct)	   1.3	0.8     0.8</p>
<p> Annual change (not s/adj, in pct)	8.8	7.9    -2.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Philip Williamson, Nationwide marketing and commmercial director said October transactions figures show the highest number of deals since 1989 suggesting a broader based recovery is now underway.</p>
<p>&quot;With rising equity values and improving confidence, more existing homeowners are now entering the market. This trend is expected to continue and should help alleviate the shortages of supply that have been an important factor this year in pushing prices higher.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
